
This directory contains a set of class templates that are defined in 
namespace Pscf::Rp and used in the program-level namespaces Pscf::Rpc 
and Rpg. Instantiated specializations of each class template in namespace 
Pscf::Rp are used as base classes for corresponding specializations of 
two closely analogous class templates defined in Pscf::Rpc and Pscf::Rpg. 
Generally, the base class template in Pscf::Rp and the derived class 
templates in Pscf::Rpc and Rpg::Rpg all share the same name. For example, 
each specialization of the template <int D> class Pscf::Rpc::System with 
an integer argument D=1, 2, or 3 is derived from a corresponding
specialization of a class template defined in the Pscf::Rp namespace 
that is also named "System". 

Types classes:

All of the templates defined in namespace Pscf::Rp take the dimension D of 
space as an integer template parameter. Most also take a class parameter 
named "T" as an additional parameter. In specializations of such templates,
the argument associated with parameter T should either be a specialization
Rpc::Types<D> defined of the template defined in src/rpc/system/Types.h, 
for specializations used used in namespace Pscf::Rpc, or a specialization 
Pscf::Rpg::Types<D> of the template defined in file src/rpg/system/Types.h, 
for specializations used in namespace Pscf::Rpg. The "Types" class templates 
defined in the Pscf::Rpc and Pscf::Rpg program-level namespaces each take 
the spatial dimension D as a single template parameter, and define a set 
of typename aliases for classes used only in the enclosing program-level 
namespace for the specified value of D. 

Typename aliases defined in each such "Types" class are used in class
templates defined in Pscf::Rp to create generic class definitions that 
can be adapted for use in either pscf_rpc or pscf_rpg by simply using 
a different "Types" class as a template argument. As an example, consider 
the class Pscf::Rpc::System<3>, which is the type of the main system 
object used in the pscf_rpc CPU program for problems involving 
three-dimensional fields. This class is a specialization of the class
template Pscf::Rpc::System<int D>, and is a subclass of a template
specialization Pscf::Rp::System<3, Pscf::Rpc::Types<3> > of the 
System class template defined in namespace Rp, using an argument 
T = Pscf::Rpc::Types<3> that contains type definitions appropriate for
use in namespace Pscf::Rpc.

Subdirectories:

The src/rp directory has the subjectories listed below, giving a 
structure analogous to that of both the src/rpc and src/rpg directories:
  
field/      - fields and spatial domain
fts/        - partial saddle-point field theoretic simulation (PS-FTS)
scft/       - self-consistent field theory (SCFT)
solvers/    - modified diffusion equation (MDE) solvers
system/     - main System class template

